firefighters made good progress on the  sandy valley fire over the weekend the  fire is now  90 percent contained it's burning below  a mountain spring summit on the  backside of the spring mountains on the  prompt side of the spring mountains  the bureau of land management says it's  burned nearly 1400 acres  about 130 firefighters were on the  ground fighting that fire  to get a handle on it it's believed to  have been caused by  target shooting a round that reportedly  caused a spark and ignited dry  vegetation  so if you plan to go out target shooting  here's some things to remember  pick a safe spot don't shoot into rocks  or vegetation  and the type of ammo you use really  matters steel  core and solid copper solid copper ammo  are most likely to start fires and are  restricted this time of year  there are fire restrictions in the  mountains always bring a  shovel some water a fire extinguisher  good ideas just in case and lastly  do not shoot on hot dry windy days when  fire risk is high that's like today  there are red flag warnings for the  mountains today
 

